 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Cash rate:** The RBA cash rate target has risen by **4.26 percentage points**, from 0.10% (January 2022 monthly average) to 4.36% (September 2026 monthly average). It rose through 2022 and 2023 to a peak of about 4.35% in late 2023. It was cut to 3.60% by late 2025, then lifted again from February 2026 to 4.36%.\n\n**Sydney rents:** Rent growth is **3.5% over the year to August 2026** (ABS CPI, rents, Sydney). That is slowing compared with its peak of 8.8% in March 2024, though it has picked up slightly from a low of 3.2% in August and September 2025. It has been between 3.3% and 3.5% since late 2025.",
